<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdallah ibn Tahir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">798–<a href="/years/845">845</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdallah ibn Tahir was the most celebrated ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahirid-dynasty">Tahirid dynasty</a>, governing Khurasan for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> from 828 to 845 from his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nishapur">Nishapur</a>. Loyal but autonomous, he sent tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> while ruling the eastern provinces in his own right. He was known for his justice, his protection of the peasantry and his regulation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qanat">qanat</a> irrigation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdallah-ibn-tahir.jpg" alt="Abdallah ibn Tahir" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ro4444 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tahirid_Khurasan_ca_836_AD.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Abdallah ibn Tahir</b> (828 to 845) was known for justice, protection of peasants and regulation of the qanat irrigation system.</blockquote><a href="/state/tahirid-dynasty">Tahirid dynasty</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nishapur">Nishapur</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nishapur">Nishapur</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=36.21,58.8&amp;year=828" aria-label="Nishapur on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6030 857 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Abdallah ibn Tahir"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6480 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6480 1127h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=36.21,58.8&amp;year=828">What was here in 828 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
